From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "qid (local patch)" <xiaohanzhaoclaude@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 06:26:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] local patch 4: handle Anthropic adaptive thinking
 (output_config.effort) field
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Anthropic API introduced adaptive thinking in Opus 4.6+ / Sonnet 4.6+,
mandatory on Opus 4.7/4.8. The new wire format replaces the legacy
`thinking.budget_tokens` (now rejected with 400 on 4.7/4.8) with:

  thinking: {type: "adaptive"}     ← enable adaptive mode
  output_config: {effort: "xhigh"} ← guide thinking depth

Patch 1 (2026-05-29) only handled the LEGACY budget_tokens path, which
silently never fired on modern Claude Code sessions. This patch
extends translateToOpenAI to also handle output_config.effort and
translates it to Copilot's `reasoning_effort` field (OpenAI-format).

Also fixes translateModelName: bare hyphenated `claude-opus-4-7`
(emitted by Claude Code when the wrapper resolves the `opus` alias
via ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7[1m] — the [1m]
suffix is stripped client-side before send) now maps to the
xhigh-capable `claude-opus-4.7-1m-internal` instead of base 4.7
(which is medium-only). Same for hyphenated 4-8.

Also adds an optional COPILOT_API_DUMP_PAYLOADS env-var gated
diagnostic that writes full request/response payloads to
/tmp/copilot-api-payloads.jsonl, bypassing journald's 48KB
line-truncation. Useful for verifying wire shape during config
changes; off by default.

Verified end-to-end 2026-06-03:

  [in-anthropic]
    model: claude-opus-4-7
    thinking: {type: "adaptive"}
    output_config: {effort: "xhigh"}
    reasoning_effort: ABSENT

  [out-openai]
    model: claude-opus-4.7-1m-internal   ← patch 3+4 routes to 1m-internal
    thinking: ABSENT                      ← stripped (Anthropic-only field)
    output_config: ABSENT                 ← stripped (translated below)
    reasoning_effort: xhigh               ← patch 4 translation

Zero 400 errors. PR daemons unaffected (they use dotted forms which
pass through unchanged). Hard math probe produces ~2KB of high-quality
multi-method reasoning — characteristic xhigh-tier output depth.

This patch combined with the wrapper's new env vars completes the
"actually-engaging-xhigh-effort-on-Copilot" goal. The wrapper now
sets:
  ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7[1m]   (1M context flag)
  ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL_SUPPORTED_CAPABILITIES=
    "effort,xhigh_effort,thinking,adaptive_thinking,interleaved_thinking"
  CLAUDE_AUTOCOMPACT_PCT_OVERRIDE=80
  --model opus
